{
  "root": true,
  "extends": "./.eslintrc.json",
  "rules": {
    "alfanumrik/no-direct-ai-calls": "error",
    "alfanumrik/no-direct-rag-rpc": "error",
    "alfanumrik/no-canonical-write-outside-projector": "error"
  },
  "overrides": [
    {
      "files": ["supabase/functions/**/*.ts"],
      "parserOptions": {
        "project": null,
        "sourceType": "module"
      }
    },

    {
      // ==================================================================
      // BLOCK 1 — CONFIG-LAYERING REPAIR. Gives up ZERO enforcement.
      // ==================================================================
      // This block restores an exemption that ALREADY EXISTS in the base
      // config and that this file was silently reversing.
      //
      // `.eslintrc.json` deliberately turns
      // `alfanumrik/no-canonical-write-outside-projector` OFF for test files
      // ("Test files may write canonical state directly"), and the RULE'S OWN
      // header documents the same decision and the same mechanism:
      //
      //   "Test fixtures (src/__tests__/**, *.test.*, *.spec.*) are turned OFF
      //    for this rule via an .eslintrc.json override [...] tests legitimately
      //    seed/clean canonical tables as E2E setup (there is no projector in a
      //    test). The rule governs the production write path."
      //
      // But ESLint applies an extending config's TOP-LEVEL `rules` AFTER the
      // extended config's `overrides`. So the `"error"` above clobbered the
      // base config's `"off"`, and this file re-enabled the rule on exactly
      // the files the base config had exempted. Measured 2026-08-31:
      //
      //   eslint --print-config apps/host/src/__tests__/migrations/canonical-mastery-e2e.test.ts
      //     base .eslintrc.json          -> ["off"]      <- intended
      //     .eslintrc.ai-boundary.json   -> ["error"]    <- the bug
      //
      // That accounted for 13 of the 35 errors this config reported. They are
      // all `.delete()` / `.insert()` E2E seed+teardown of `concept_mastery`
      // in migration tests — the exact case the base config already blessed.
      //
      // The `files` list is a VERBATIM copy of the base config's block, so the
      // enforced scope is byte-identical to what the base config already
      // intends. Do not widen it here — widen it in `.eslintrc.json` and copy
      // the change across, or the two will drift again.
      //
      // DURABLE FIX (owner: whoever owns this file): move the three strict
      // severities out of the top-level `rules` above and into an override
      // scoped to production paths, so the base config's test exemptions are
      // never re-armed by layering order. Not done here because it changes the
      // resolution order for every rule at once and wants its own review.
      "files": [
        "apps/*/src/__tests__/**",
        "apps/*/src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}",
        "apps/*/src/**/*.spec.{ts,tsx}",
        "packages/*/src/__tests__/**",
        "packages/*/src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}",
        "packages/*/src/**/*.spec.{ts,tsx}"
      ],
      "rules": {
        "alfanumrik/no-canonical-write-outside-projector": "off"
      }
    },

    {
      // ==================================================================
      // BLOCK 2 — NEW, NARROW EXEMPTION: no-direct-ai-calls in TEST FILES.
      // This one DOES give up enforcement. Read the justification.
      // ==================================================================
      // `alfanumrik/no-direct-ai-calls` fires on any string literal matching
      // /api\.(anthropic|voyageai)\.com/ ANYWHERE in a file — it does not and
      // cannot distinguish a live `fetch()` from a mock, a fixture, a recorded
      // cassette key, a simulated DNS error, or an assertion ABOUT the
      // boundary. In a test file it is only ever the latter: nothing in this
      // repo's suite makes a live provider call (vitest + Deno tests run
      // offline; the edge-function CI job is explicitly "deterministic,
      // offline"). The rule's purpose — one choke point for grounding,
      // citation, PII redaction and circuit-breaker policy on the PRODUCTION
      // call path — has no test-file surface to protect.
      //
      // This was verified PER FILE, not assumed. All 11 test hits as of
      // 2026-08-31, and what each actually is:
      //
      //   apps/host/src/__tests__/foxy-remediation-oracle-shape.test.ts:215,331
      //   apps/host/src/__tests__/foxy-remediation-output-safety.test.ts:150,469
      //     -> `fetchSpy.mock.calls.filter(url => url.includes('api.anthropic.com'))`
      //        NEGATIVE ASSERTIONS that Anthropic is NOT called (or called
      //        exactly once via the sanctioned path). :469 even carries the
      //        comment "that is what the alfanumrik/no-direct-ai-calls rule
      //        enforces". The rule was failing the tests that enforce it.
      //
      //   apps/host/src/__tests__/foxy-rerank-fallback.test.ts:68
      //     -> rerank call driven by an INJECTED `fetchImpl` (a `vi.fn()`),
      //        never global fetch.
      //   apps/host/src/__tests__/foxy-rerank-fallback.test.ts:167
      //     -> the string "ENOTFOUND api.voyageai.com" inside
      //        `mockRejectedValue(new Error(...))` — a simulated DNS failure.
      //
      //   apps/host/src/__tests__/regressions/rag-confidence-v2-shadow-source-pins.test.ts:389
      //     -> a SOURCE-PIN assertion: reads supabase/functions/_shared/
      //        reranking.ts (an ALLOWLISTED file) and asserts its text still
      //        contains `const RERANK_ENDPOINT = '...'`. The URL is quoted
      //        evidence about blessed production source.
      //
      //   supabase/functions/_shared/mol/__tests__/cassette-helper.test.ts:51,130,385
      //     -> :51 a fixture request object for the VCR-style cassette
      //        recorder; :130 two URL strings compared to prove the request
      //        hash changes; :385 a call made after `globalThis.fetch` is
      //        replaced by a stub on the preceding lines.
      //
      //   supabase/functions/alfabot-answer/__tests__/integration.test.ts:52
      //     -> `if (url.includes('api.voyageai.com'))` inside a fetch
      //        INTERCEPTOR that returns a canned embedding.
      //
      // SCOPE IS TEST PATHS ONLY — never a directory. In particular this does
      // NOT exempt `supabase/functions/**`: that directory is the rule's
      // PRIMARY jurisdiction, and the seven production violations there and in
      // packages/lib are tracked in scripts/ai-boundary-baseline.json, not
      // exempted. See that file's header.
      //
      // The supabase globs are additive relative to Block 1 (the base config's
      // test globs only cover apps/* and packages/*, because .eslintrc.json's
      // lint scope never reached supabase/functions until this gate did).
      "files": [
        "apps/*/src/__tests__/**",
        "apps/*/src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}",
        "apps/*/src/**/*.spec.{ts,tsx}",
        "packages/*/src/__tests__/**",
        "packages/*/src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}",
        "packages/*/src/**/*.spec.{ts,tsx}",
        "supabase/functions/**/__tests__/**",
        "supabase/functions/**/*.test.ts"
      ],
      "rules": {
        "alfanumrik/no-direct-ai-calls": "off"
      }
    }
  ]
}
